# --- fork addition (khunmax2/Upstream_Deeptutor) ---------------------------
# Baseline for every tracked file: normalise to LF in the repository and check
# out LF on every platform, so a Windows clone does not turn 984 frontend files
# into CRLF and fail `prettier --check` (web/.prettierrc pins endOfLine: "lf").
# Upstream's per-extension rules below already did this for .py/.sh/.md/.json/
# .yaml/.toml but never covered .ts/.tsx/.mjs/.css/.js.
#
# Order matters: later lines win, so this wildcard must come FIRST and every
# binary type must be re-excluded after it. One tracked fixture
# (tests/fixtures/.../_origin.pdf) is stored with CRLF and git's auto-detection
# reads it as text — without the `-text` guards below, adding this line would
# renormalise and corrupt it.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png -text
*.jpg -text
*.jpeg -text
*.gif -text
*.ico -text
*.pdf -text
*.woff -text
*.woff2 -text
*.ttf -text
*.otf -text
*.zip -text
*.gz -text
# --- end fork addition -----------------------------------------------------

*.mp4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Force critical build and script files to use LF line endings for cross-platform compatibility
# This prevents CRLF-related security issues in Docker containers and shell scripts
Dockerfile text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml text eol=lf
docker-compose.*.yml text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.env text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.cfg text eol=lf
*.ini text eol=lf
